    "title": "common: Skip environment locale check on illumos",
    "user": {
      "login": "hebasto",
      "id": 32963518,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYzNTE4",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32963518?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hebasto",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "On illumos-based distributions whose GCC is built with the `--enable-clocale=dragonfly` option (e.g. OmniOS, OpenIndiana), the `std::ctype<char>::~ctype()` destructor passes an uninitialized value to `freelocale()`.\r\n\r\nConstructing and destroying `std::locale(\"\")` in `SetupEnvironment()` therefore intermittently crashes, e.g. with \"libc thread failure: lfree() called with a misaligned pointer\".\r\n\r\nUpstream reports:\r\n- https://github.com/illumos/gcc/pull/56#issuecomment-5933176361\r\n- https://github.com/omniosorg/omnios-build/issues/4253\r\n- https://www.illumos.org/issues/18481\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/hebasto/bitcoin-core-nightly/issues/315.",
