      "message": "common: Skip environment locale check on illumos\n\nOn illumos-based distributions whose GCC is built with the\n`--enable-clocale=dragonfly` option (e.g. OmniOS, OpenIndiana), the\n`std::ctype<char>::~ctype()` destructor passes an uninitialized value\nto `freelocale()`.\n\nConstructing and destroying `std::locale(\"\")` in `SetupEnvironment()`\ntherefore intermittently crashes, e.g. with \"libc thread failure:\nlfree() called with a misaligned pointer\".\n\nUpstream reports:\n- https://github.com/illumos/gcc/pull/56#issuecomment-5933176361\n- https://github.com/omniosorg/omnios-build/issues/4253\n- https://www.illumos.org/issues/18481",
